# ── Layout ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#   game/    EXACTLY what deploys. Upload this folder and nothing else.
#   source/  authoring originals (.glb sculpts, the music library). NOT shipped,
#            and mostly NOT tracked — see below. Back this up separately.
#   tools/   build scripts + the local dev server.
#   docs/    plans and notes.
#
# git here is for the CODE and the RUNTIME assets that make it run. Source art is
# binary, effectively static, does not need per-line history, and makes every git
# command crawl.
#
# 2026-07-18: game assets and sfx ARE tracked. They were ignored once, so a GitHub
# zip arrived with no models and no sound and the game could not run. Keep them in.
#
# 2026-07-24: site flattened, then restructured into game/ + source/ + tools/.
# The unused music libraries moved to source/audio/ and the .glb sculpts belong in
# source/glb/ — both excluded here. sound/sfx/ lives in game/ and stays TRACKED:
# it is the only audio index.html loads, and excluding it reintroduces the silent-
# game bug above.

# ── source art: large, binary, backed up outside git ──
# palm_tree.glb alone is 233 MB — over GitHub's 100 MB per-file hard limit, which
# would make the push fail outright. The audio library is ~646 MB and unreferenced.
source/glb/
source/audio/
*.glb

# NOTE: source/wip/ is deliberately NOT ignored. It is work-in-progress voxel art
# kept out of game/ so it never deploys, but still tracked so it has a backup.

# ── legacy / scratch ──
# tools/frames/ is the frame-capture dump the video export writes (snap<timestamp> (NNNN).png).
# 120 stills of one clip is ~29 MB and it regenerates on demand — same reasoning as _snapshots/.
tools/frames/
# serve-nocache.py imports tools/bundle.py, so Python writes bytecode next to it
tools/__pycache__/
art/
.vox/
website_old/
_snapshots/
*.bak
*.log
node_modules/
